{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792410245,"nonce":"TvmV7bb3h7oyyTTxuVOjjgIB+30=","message":"Element-frame clip paths are in 5b2d18eb9e1d0d1bebaaf33fb28acd4124af8819 (local, not pushed). GpuPrimitive::clip_shape points to an aux_data payload containing the inverse screen-to-element frame, logical translation/kind/radius and shape parameters. Polygon points follow, two per row, with their offset relative to the header. The frame divides its linear part by display scale; its geometry and translation remain in logical units. Run merging rebases one pointer, and drawing into a layer texture translates each distinct payload's frame once. The primitive is now 34 vec4 fields, 544 bytes; all twelve copies and layout guards agree.\n\nThe shared binding-dependent shader helper is composed after declarations and before the fragment entry; its DT form reads through load_aux. It covers ellipses, rounded rectangles and polygons, with explicit closing edges, 1e30 ring separators, nonzero/even-odd winding and the producer's four-probe coverage override. Boxes, glyphs, shadows and notches take the clip. Images remain ClipShape. Record::to_primitive also reports ClipShape for a shape requiring auxiliary data; primitive, decode and plan carry those rows. The shared ClipPath enum, CSS keyword and ABI schema remain unchanged.\n\nFixtures came from blinc_abi a92f5c0's encoder. GPU-free decode, truncated-polygon, gradient/shape offset and flattened-layer rebasing tests pass. Offscreen Apple M1 Pro, Metal: all 22 display-list tests and the polygon clip test pass on the storage-buffer path. Forcing the vertex-buffer path also passes all 22. At scales 1 and 2, eleven new scenes cover all three shapes, equal-orientation rings under both rules, a general affine, inherited clips under a different child transform, an outer shadow, a notch, a rotated filtered layer with a conic table, and payload rebasing when an unsupported masked layer is flattened. Worst channel error against the independent CPU oracle is 1/255; clipped glyphs match exactly. Removing clip-frame translation fails by 204/255.\n\nOracle detail: the producer's polygon four-probe override jumps when the final probe crosses an edge. The initial rotated-layer comparison differed by 6/255 at a probe within 0.001 logical pixels of an edge because interpolation rounding changes that override. The shader formula was retained. The oracle excludes only such boundary probes, capped below 200 pixels per scene: 2 of 24,000 pixels at scale 1 and 13 of 96,000 at scale 2 for the rotated layer; all other new scenes skip none. The glyph test helper now uploads decoded auxiliary rows, which shape clips require.\n\nGate: fmt, workspace clippy, 1,885 workspace nextest tests (48 skipped), docs with warnings denied, wasm, iOS and threaded layout/CN tests pass. The separate DSL run has 516 passed, 28 failed, 10 skipped; every failing name matches the untouched ff83adca baseline already recorded under a33d2b9. No dependency or DSL sources changed. PowerVR/Adreno shader compilation and mobile pixels remain unverified; ce34b20 still tracks stale DT packing. Next: image clipping, where local clips, fading clips and clip-path frames still need pipeline support.","files":null}]}